# anode_physical: Li-metal half cell (same lattice and mechanism as the original
# engine) with PHYSICALLY BASED anode kinetics (docs/KINETICS_TABLE.md).
# The legacy case stays byte-identical; this is a new reference, validated
# against experiment (CE 0.995 to 0.999, Yu et al. Nat. Energy 2022, Fig. 4)
# and against the original run as antecedent (morphology, SEI growth).
seed 8597
temperature 298
saltMolar 1.2
solvMolar 6.5
scanIntervalType time
potentialType step
scanInterval 3600
maxInterval 50
BeginV 4.4
EndV 2.8
totalSteps 100000
maxCycles 152
printStepFreq 1
XYZprintFreq 100
snapshotEveryCycles 20
checkpointEveryCycles 20
globalA 0.5
numberDecompositionRxns 6
nMobilityReactions 3
# ---- Li inventory: finite anode (2026-09-24) ---------------------------------
# li_pool_mode shared + li_bulk_init 0: the Li+ pool is the only Li source for
# plating, stripping returns Li+ to it, and the framework fill may NOT create
# Li from a semi-infinite foil. In run 1 (legacy fixed mode) the foil refilled
# every stripped vacancy while plating added on top, so the slab grew 1150 ->
# 6100 sites with zero net plating and filled the whole box by half-cycle
# 116-151 (4 of 5 seeds stalled: no electrolyte-facing site left). The original
# C++ engine shows the same growth (2266 -> 8948); it is kept as the antecedent.
li_pool_mode shared
li_bulk_init 0
# ---- physically based anode kinetics (opt-in) -----------------------------
# k0_site = j0 * A_site / e with j0 = 29.8 mA/cm2 (LiFSI in DME, Boyle et al.
# ACS Energy Lett. 2020, 5, 701, Table 1) and A_site = (2.0 A)^2 -> 74 s^-1.
# alpha 0.5 (Butler-Volmer at low overpotential, Boyle 2020 Fig. 2).
# eta = +-30 mV: working choice for C/10 to C/5 (to be replaced by the group's
# Li||Cu polarization data; tag [P] in KINETICS_TABLE.md).
anode_kinetics bv
bv_k0_site 74
bv_alpha 0.5
eta_charge -0.03
eta_discharge 0.03
